Software Requirements Specification (SRS)
Project: College Campus Management System
1. Abstract
The College Campus Management System is a software application developed to manage and organize college activities efficiently. It helps manage student information, faculty details, attendance, examinations, fees, and other academic activities.

The system reduces manual paperwork, saves time, improves data accuracy, and provides easy access to college information. It allows students, faculty, and administrators to perform their tasks through a centralized system.

2. Identification of Users
1. Admin

The admin manages the complete college system. The admin can manage students, faculty, departments, courses, and monitor overall college activities.

2. Student

The student can log in to the system, view personal details, check attendance, view examination results, access the timetable, and check fee details.

3. Faculty

The faculty can manage attendance, enter student marks, view student details, and manage academic activities.

4. HOD (Head of Department)

The HOD manages department activities, monitors faculty and students, and checks academic performance.

5. Accountant

The accountant manages student fees, payment records, and financial information.

6. Librarian

The librarian manages books, library records, and book issue and return activities.

3. Functional Requirements
Functional requirements describe what the College Campus Management System should do.

FR1: User Registration

The system should allow the admin to register students and faculty by providing necessary details.

FR2: User Login

The system should allow students, faculty, and administrators to log in using valid credentials.

FR3: Student Management

The system should allow authorized users to add, view, update, and manage student information.

FR4: Faculty Management

The system should allow the admin to add, update, and manage faculty details such as name, department, and contact information.

FR5: Department Management

The system should allow the admin to create and manage departments and assign faculty members to departments.

FR6: Course Management

The system should allow the admin to manage courses, subjects, and academic information.

FR7: Attendance Management

The system should allow faculty to record and view student attendance.

FR8: Timetable Management

The system should allow the admin to create and manage class timetables.

FR9: Examination Management

The system should allow faculty to manage examinations and enter student marks.

FR10: Result Management

The system should allow students to view their examination results.

FR11: Fee Management

The system should allow the accountant to manage student fees and record payments.

FR12: Library Management

The system should allow the librarian to manage books and maintain book issue and return records.

FR13: Notice Management

The system should allow the admin or faculty to publish important college announcements and notices.

FR14: Report Generation

The system should generate reports related to students, attendance, examination results, and fee payments.

FR15: User Management

The system should allow the admin to manage user accounts and assign access permissions.

FR16: Logout

The system should allow users to securely log out from the application.

4. Non-Functional Requirements
Non-functional requirements describe how the application should work and its quality.

NFR1: Performance

The system should respond quickly to user requests and display college information without unnecessary delays.

NFR2: Security

The system should protect student and faculty information from unauthorized access.

NFR3: Usability

The application should be simple, user-friendly, and easy to understand.

NFR4: Reliability

The system should provide accurate and consistent student, attendance, and examination information.

NFR5: Availability

The system should be available whenever students and college staff need it, except during maintenance.

NFR6: Data Backup

The system should maintain backups of important college information to prevent data loss.

NFR7: Privacy

Student and faculty information should be accessible only to authorized users.

NFR8: Maintainability

The system should be easy to update, modify, and maintain.

NFR9: Scalability

The system should support an increasing number of students, faculty members, and departments.

NFR10: Compatibility

The application should work properly on supported computers and web browsers.

5. Modules of the College Campus Management System
Modules are the main parts of the application. Each module performs a specific college-related task.

1. Admin Module

The Admin Module manages the complete college system. It allows the admin to manage students, faculty, departments, courses, and college activities.

2. Student Module

The Student Module handles student registration, profile management, and student academic information.

3. Faculty Module

The Faculty Module manages faculty details and allows faculty members to perform academic activities.

4. Department Module

The Department Module manages department information, courses, and faculty assignments.

5. Attendance Module

The Attendance Module records and monitors student attendance. It allows faculty to mark attendance and students to view their attendance percentage.

6. Timetable Module

The Timetable Module creates and manages class schedules. It helps students and faculty view their daily and weekly timetables.

7. Examination Module

The Examination Module manages examinations, marks, and student results.

8. Fee Module

The Fee Module manages student fee details, payment records, and pending fee information.

9. Library Module

The Library Module manages books, book availability, and book issue and return activities.

10. Notice Module

The Notice Module allows the college to publish announcements, exam notifications, and important information.

11. Report Module

The Report Module generates reports related to student details, attendance, examination results, and fee payments.

12. Database Module

The Database Module stores and manages all college-related information, including student details, faculty information, attendance, examination records, and fee details.

6. Conclusion
The College Campus Management System provides an efficient way to manage college activities through a computerized system. It reduces manual work, improves communication, and helps students, faculty, and administrators access information easily. The system makes academic and administrative activities more organized, accurate, and convenient.




