Project: Online Food Ordering System
1. Abstract
The Online Food Ordering System is a web-based application developed to make food ordering easy and convenient. It allows customers to view food items, select their favorite dishes, add them to the cart, and place orders online.

The system helps restaurants manage food items, customer orders, and payments efficiently. It reduces manual work, saves time, and provides a simple and user-friendly way to order food.
2. Identification of Users
1. Admin

The admin manages the complete application. The admin can manage users, restaurants, food items, and monitor overall system activities.

2. Customer

The customer can register, log in, view food items, search for food, add items to the cart, place orders, make payments, and track orders.

3. Restaurant Manager

The restaurant manager can manage restaurant details, add or update food items, view customer orders, and update order status.

4. Delivery Person

The delivery person can view assigned orders, collect food from the restaurant, deliver it to customers, and update delivery status.
3. Functional Requirements
Functional requirements describe what the application should do.

FR1: User Registration

The system should allow customers to create an account by providing necessary details such as name, email, phone number, and password.

FR2: User Login

The system should allow registered users to log in using valid credentials.

FR3: Food Menu

The system should display available food items with their names, prices, images, and descriptions.

FR4: Food Search

The system should allow customers to search for food items by name.

FR5: Food Categories

The system should display food items based on categories such as pizza, burgers, biryani, and drinks.

FR6: Cart Management

The system should allow customers to add food items to the cart, remove items, and change quantities.

FR7: Order Placement

The system should allow customers to place orders by selecting food items and providing a delivery address.

FR8: Order Management

The system should allow restaurant managers to view customer orders and accept or reject them.

FR9: Payment Management

The system should allow customers to pay for their orders using available payment methods such as online payment or cash on delivery.

FR10: Order Tracking

The system should allow customers to view the status of their orders, such as pending, accepted, preparing, out for delivery, and delivered.

FR11: Food Management

The system should allow restaurant managers to add, update, and delete food items from the menu.

FR12: Delivery Management

The system should allow delivery persons to view assigned orders and update the delivery status.

FR13: Order History

The system should allow customers to view their previous orders and order details.

FR14: Feedback and Rating

The system should allow customers to provide feedback and ratings for food items or restaurants.

FR15: Logout

The system should allow users to securely log out from the application.
4. Non-Functional Requirements
Non-functional requirements describe how the application should work and its quality.

NFR1: Performance

The application should respond quickly to user requests and display food items without unnecessary delays.

NFR2: Security

The system should protect user accounts and prevent unauthorized access.

NFR3: Usability

The application should be simple, user-friendly, and easy to understand.

NFR4: Reliability

The system should process orders and payments accurately without frequent errors.

NFR5: Availability

The application should be available whenever customers want to order food, except during maintenance.

NFR6: Scalability

The system should support an increasing number of customers, restaurants, and orders.

NFR7: Data Backup

The system should maintain backups of important information to prevent data loss.

NFR8: Compatibility

The application should work properly on supported web browsers and devices.

NFR9: Maintainability

The system should be easy to update, modify, and maintain.

NFR10: Privacy

The system should protect customer personal information and allow access only to authorized users.
5. Modules of the Online Food Ordering System
Modules are the main parts of the application. Each module performs a specific task.

1. Admin Module

The Admin Module manages the complete application. It allows the admin to manage users, restaurants, food items, and monitor system activities.

2. Customer Module

The Customer Module handles customer registration, login, profile management, and customer information.

3. Food Menu Module

The Food Menu Module displays food items, prices, images, descriptions, and food categories. It allows customers to browse available food.

4. Cart Module

The Cart Module stores the food items selected by customers before placing an order. It allows customers to add, remove, and update food quantities.

5. Order Module

The Order Module manages customer orders. It handles order placement, order confirmation, and order status updates.

6. Payment Module

The Payment Module manages customer payments. It records payment details and supports available payment methods.

7. Delivery Module

The Delivery Module manages food delivery activities. It allows delivery persons to view assigned orders and update delivery status.

8. Feedback Module

The Feedback Module allows customers to provide ratings and reviews about food items and restaurants.

9. Database Module

The Database Module stores and manages customer details, food items, restaurant information, orders, payments, and delivery records.
6. Conclusion
The Online Food Ordering System provides a convenient way for customers to order food online. It helps restaurants manage food menus and customer orders efficiently. The system reduces manual work, saves time, improves order management, and provides a better food ordering experience for customers.


