Software Requirements Specification (SRS)
Project: Hospital Management System
1. Abstract
The Hospital Management System is a software application developed to manage hospital activities efficiently. It helps manage patient details, doctor information, appointments, medical records, medicines, and billing.

The system reduces manual paperwork, saves time, improves data accuracy, and makes hospital operations easier. It provides a centralized platform where doctors, patients, and hospital staff can access and manage information.

2. Identification of Users
1. Admin

The admin manages the complete hospital system. The admin can manage users, doctors, departments, and monitor overall hospital activities.

2. Doctor

The doctor can view patient details, examine patients, record diagnosis, prescribe medicines, and maintain medical records.

3. Patient
The patient can register, log in, view doctor details, book appointments, view medical records, and check bills.

4. Receptionist
The receptionist manages patient registration, appointment booking, and patient information.

5. Nurse
The nurse can view patient details, assist doctors, and maintain basic patient care information.

6. Pharmacist

The pharmacist manages medicines, medicine availability, and pharmacy stock.

7. Accountant

The accountant manages hospital bills, patient payments, and financial records.

3. Functional Requirements
Functional requirements describe what the Hospital Management System should do.

FR1: User Registration

The system should allow patients to register by providing necessary details such as name, age, contact number, and address.

FR2: User Login

The system should allow authorized users to log in using valid credentials.

FR3: Patient Management

The system should allow authorized users to add, view, update, and manage patient information.

FR4: Doctor Management

The system should allow the admin to add, update, and manage doctor details such as name, specialization, and contact information.

FR5: Appointment Management

The system should allow patients or receptionists to book, view, and cancel appointments with doctors.

FR6: Medical Records Management

The system should allow doctors to maintain patient diagnosis, treatment details, and medical history.

FR7: Prescription Management

The system should allow doctors to create and maintain prescriptions for patients.

FR8: Medicine Management

The system should allow pharmacists to add, update, and manage medicines and their stock availability.

FR9: Billing Management

The system should generate bills for consultations, treatments, medicines, and other hospital services.

FR10: Payment Management

The system should allow authorized users to record and manage patient payments.

FR11: Patient History

The system should allow doctors to view the previous medical history of patients.

FR12: Report Generation

The system should generate reports related to patients, appointments, medicines, and billing.

FR13: User Management

The system should allow the admin to manage user accounts and assign access permissions.

FR14: Logout

The system should allow users to securely log out from the application.

4. Non-Functional Requirements
Non-functional requirements describe how the application should work and its quality.

NFR1: Performance

The system should respond quickly to user requests and display hospital information without unnecessary delays.

NFR2: Security

The system should protect patient information and prevent unauthorized access.

NFR3: Usability

The application should be simple, user-friendly, and easy to understand.

NFR4: Reliability

The system should provide accurate and consistent patient, appointment, and billing information.

NFR5: Availability

The system should be available whenever hospital staff need it, except during maintenance.

NFR6: Data Backup

The system should maintain backups of important hospital information to prevent data loss.

NFR7: Privacy

Patient medical records should be accessible only to authorized users.

NFR8: Maintainability

The system should be easy to update, modify, and maintain.

NFR9: Scalability

The system should support an increasing number of patients, doctors, and hospital staff.

NFR10: Compatibility

The application should work properly on supported computers and web browsers.

5. Modules of the Hospital Management System
Modules are the main parts of the application. Each module performs a specific hospital-related task.

1. Admin Module

The Admin Module manages the complete hospital system. It allows the admin to manage users, doctors, departments, and hospital activities.

2. Patient Module

The Patient Module handles patient registration, profile management, and patient information.

3. Doctor Module

The Doctor Module manages doctor details, specialization, availability, and patient treatment information.

4. Appointment Module

The Appointment Module manages patient appointments. It allows patients to book appointments and helps receptionists manage doctor schedules.

5. Medical Records Module

The Medical Records Module stores patient diagnosis, treatment details, medical history, and prescriptions.

6. Pharmacy Module

The Pharmacy Module manages medicines, medicine details, stock availability, and medicine records.

7. Billing Module

The Billing Module generates patient bills for consultations, treatments, medicines, and other hospital services.

8. Payment Module

The Payment Module records patient payments and maintains payment information.

9. Report Module

The Report Module generates reports related to patients, appointments, medicines, and hospital billing.

10. Database Module

The Database Module stores and manages all hospital-related information, including patient details, doctor information, appointments, medical records, and billing data.

6. Conclusion
The Hospital Management System provides an efficient way to manage hospital activities through a computerized system. It reduces manual paperwork, improves data management, and helps doctors, patients, and hospital staff perform their tasks easily. The system makes hospital operations more organized, accurate, and convenient.
